"Listen on Amazon Alexa Tablets (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-on-amazon-alexa-tablets)\nciteturn1002view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":3}); Total lines: 148\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Listening Ways to listen\nL13: ## Listen on Amazon Alexa Tablets\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 8, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen on Amazon Alexa Tablets\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-on-amazon-alexa-tablets\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Audible comes built in on the new Amazon Alexa Tablets, so you can start listening from the first time you turn on your device. Sign in with your Amazon account, and your Library, listening progress, and recommendations are ready to go.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†How do I get started with Audible on my Alexa Tablet?】\nL32:   * 【2†Where can I find my audiobooks on my Alexa Tablet?】\nL33:   * 【3†What additional listening features does my Alexa Tablet support?】\nL34:   * 【4†Can I continue listening on my other devices?】\nL35:   * 【5†Can I use Alexa with Audible on my tablet?】\nL36:   * 【6†Can I buy audiobooks on my Alexa Tablet?】\nL37:   * 【7†Can my kids listen to Audible on an Amazon Kids Tablet?】\nL38:   * 【8†Where is Audible available on Alexa Tablets?】\nL39: \nL40: Supported devices:\nL41:   * Amazon Alexa Tablet 8\nL42:   * Amazon Alexa Tablet 11\nL43:   * Amazon Alexa Tablet 12 Pro\nL44:   * Amazon Alexa Tablet 12 Pro with Nanomatte Display\nL45:   * Amazon Kids Tablets (through Amazon Kids+)\nL46: \nL47: Note: Audible and your Alexa Tablet must be linked to the same Amazon account.\nL48: ## How do I get started with Audible on my Amazon Alexa Tablet?\nL49: \nL50: The Audible app comes pre-installed on every Alexa Tablet. To start listening:\nL51: \nL52:   1. During device setup, sign in with the Amazon account you use for Audible.\nL53:   2. Open the Audible app from your Tablet Home screen.\nL54:   3. Your Library loads automatically. Tap any title to start listening.\nL55: \nL56: If you don't have an Audible membership, you can start a membership later in the Audible app.\nL57: ## Where can I find my audiobooks on my Alexa Tablet?\nL58: \nL59: Along with the Audible app, your audiobooks show up across your tablet's Home screen:\nL60: \nL61: Where  | What you'll see\nL62: --- | ---\nL63: Continue Listening Widget  | Pick up from where you left off on your titles\nL64: App Home Widget  | Resume listening in one tap without opening the app\nL65: For You tab  | The title you're listening to, so you can pick up where you left off\nL66: Books tab  | Continue Listening on Audible carousel and recommendations based on what you listen to\nL67: To add the Audible widget:\nL68: \nL69:   * Press and hold an empty space on your Home screen.\nL70:   * Select Widgets.\nL71:   * Find Audible, then drag the widget to your Home screen.\nL72: ## What additional listening features does my Alexa Tablet support?\nL73: \nL74: Dolby Atmos\nL75: Amazon Alexa Tablet 11, Amazon Alexa Tablet 12 Pro, and Amazon Alexa Tablet 12 Pro with Nanomatte Display support Dolby Atmos playback that provides a spatial sound experience. Learn more about how to 【9†Listen in Dolby Atmos】.\nL76: Read & Listen\nL77: You can listen to an audiobook while reading the Kindle book, with each word highlighted as it's read. The larger tablet screen works in both portrait and landscape. You need both the Kindle book and the Audible audiobook in your Library. Learn more about 【10†Read & Listen】.\nL78: ## Can I continue listening on my other devices?\nL79: \nL80: Yes. Audible syncs your place across your devices. If you start a title on your phone, Echo device, or car, you can pick up at the same spot on your Alexa Tablet, and the other way around. Make sure each device has an internet connection so your progress can sync.\nL81: ## Can I use Alexa with Audible on my tablet?\nL82: \nL83: Yes. In supported countries you can control Audible hands-free with Alexa+. Go to the app Settings > Alexa where you can enable Hands-Free with Alexa and Show Alexa button. For the full list of voice commands and to set up Alexa in the Audible app, see 【11†Listen with Alexa】.\nL84: ## Can I buy audiobooks on my Alexa Tablet?\nL85: \nL86: Yes. You can browse, use credits, and buy titles right in the Audible app. If you've turned on purchase protection for your device, you'll be asked to enter your password before you complete a purchase.\nL87: ## Can my kids listen to Audible on an Amazon Kids Tablet?\nL88: \nL89: Yes. Kids can listen to age-appropriate audiobooks through Amazon Kids+ on Amazon Kids Tablets. Parents can add titles from their own Audible Library and manage content in the 【12†Amazon Parent Dashboard†parents.amazon.com】.\nL90: ## Where is Audible available on Alexa Tablets?\nL91: \nL92: Audible on Alexa Tablets is available in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Germany, France, Italy, Spain, Japan, and Mexico. Some features, such as Alexa and Read & Listen, may vary by country. Alexa Tablets Help Center links 【13†here.】\nL93: \nL94: Did this answer your question?\nL95: \nL96: 【14†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL97: \nL98: \nL99: \nL100: 【15†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL101: \nL102:  Back to top\nL103: \nL104: 【16†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL105: \nL106: 【17†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL107: ## Need more assistance?\nL108: \nL109: 【18†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL110: \nL111: \nL112: \nL113: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL114: \nL115: \nL116: \nL117: Worst\nL118: \nL119: 1\nL120: \nL121: 2\nL122: \nL123: 3\nL124: \nL125: 4\nL126: \nL127: 5\nL128: \nL129: 6\nL130: \nL131: 7\nL132: \nL133: Best\nL134: \nL135: \nL136: \nL137: Region\nL138: \nL139: United States\nL140: \nL141: Language\nL142: \nL143: English\nL144: \nL145: Loading\nL146: \nL147: Listen on Amazon Alexa Tablets 【19†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen with AudibleSync (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-audiblesync)\nciteturn1002view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn998view0\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 134\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Accessibility Ask A Question AudibleSync Listening+3\nL13: ## Listen with AudibleSync\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 1, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Listen with AudibleSync\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-with-audiblesync\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: The AudibleSync app is a 【1†Windows 10 and 11 app】 for your computer that allows you to 【2†download titles】 quickly and easily to supported MP3 devices and accessibility devices.\nL29: \nL30: \nL31: In this article:\nL32:   * 【3†How do I download AudibleSync?】\nL33:   * 【4†How do I sign in to the AudibleSync app?】\nL34:   * 【5†How do I download a title in the AudibleSync app?】\nL35:   * 【6†How do I activate an MP3 player in the AudibleSync app?】\nL36:   * 【7†How do I transfer a title using the AudibleSync app?】\nL37: ## How do I download AudibleSync?\nL38: \nL39:   1. Download the 【8†AudibleSync app†d34c1xl6owclq9.cloudfront.net】.\nL40:   2. Open the downloaded file.\nL41: \nL42: ## How do I sign in to the AudibleSync app?\nL43: \nL44:   1. Open the AudibleSync app.\nL45:   2. Select Sign in.\nL46:   3. Enter your Amazon account information.\nL47: ## How do I download a title in the AudibleSync app?\nL48: \nL49: You will need to download a title in the AudibleSync app before transferring it to your MP3 player.\nL50: \nL51:   1. Open the AudibleSync app.\nL52:   2. Sign in to your account.\nL53:   3. Next to the title you’d like to download, select Download.\nL54: \nL55: Notes:\nL56:   * Once a title has finished downloading, the Download button will no longer appear.\nL57:   * Downloading titles using AudibleSync will save them to your computer but can only be played by transferring them to a compatible MP3 player or accessibility device.\nL58: ## How do I activate an MP3 player in the AudibleSync app?\nL59: \nL60: You must activate your accessibility device before you can use the AudibleSync app. This can only be done using a Windows 10 or 11 computer.\nL61: \nL62:   1. Open the AudibleSync app.\nL63:   2. Sign in to your account.\nL64:   3. Connect the device to your computer.\nL65:   4. Select the device icon.\nL66:   5. Select Activate Device.\nL67:   6. Enter your Amazon account information.\nL68: ## How do I transfer a title using the AudibleSync app?\nL69: \nL70: You can download Audible audiobooks to compatible MP3 devices and accessibility devices by following these steps:\nL71: \nL72:   1. Open the AudibleSync app.\nL73:   2. Sign in to your account.\nL74:   3. Download the title you want to transfer.\nL75:   4. Connect your accessibility device to your computer.\nL76:   5. Select the title.\nL77:   6. Select Copy to Device or drag and drop the title into the device.\nL78: Note: To review the compatible devices, please visit 【9†Devices compatible with Audible】.\nL79: \nL80: Did this answer your question?\nL81: \nL82: 【10†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL83: \nL84: \nL85: \nL86: 【11†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL87: \nL88:  Back to top\nL89: \nL90: 【12†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL91: \nL92: 【13†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL93: ## Need more assistance?\nL94: \nL95: 【14†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL96: \nL97: \nL98: \nL99: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL100: \nL101: \nL102: \nL103: Worst\nL104: \nL105: 1\nL106: \nL107: 2\nL108: \n